WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:18.140
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones successor
show that will air in 2022 on HBO.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.570
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.230
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:31.610
It is based on George RR Martin’s Targaryen
history book Fire And Blood volume 1 and on

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.450
Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume
2 book.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:38.880
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.489
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:48.719
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:53.429
The man who started it all, King Aegon I Targaryen,
known as Aegon the Conqueror

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:58.559
and Aegon the Dragon, was the founder and
the first king of the Targaryen dynasty which

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:04.330
lasted for 300 years when he conquered all
of Westeros and united the realm

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.480
(with the exception of Dorne and the lands
beyond the Wall)

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:13.380
with 2 sister-wives and their three great
dragons, Balerion, Vhagar and Meraxes.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:19.020
Aegon's dragon was Balerion the Black Dread,
the largest dragon ever seen in Westeros.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.890
Balerion's jaws were so large that he could
swallow a mammoth.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.070
Aegon was a child of House Targaryen, dwelling
on the island of Dragonstone in the Narrow

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.170
Sea.
The Targaryens, a family of Valyrian origin,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.640
had been in control of Dragonstone for a century
before the Doom of Valyria destroyed their

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.590
homeland in a volcanic cataclysm.
For another hundred years on Dragonstone,

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:45.009
the Targaryens slowly built up their strength
and raised their dragons, the last in the

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.280
world.
Aegon was born on Dragonstone in 27 BC to

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.840
Lord Aerion Targaryen and Lady Valaena Velaryon.
All of the previous six generations of Targaryens

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.250
born on Dragonstone were the product of incestuous
marriages, but Aerion had no sisters - although

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.659
by marrying a Velaryon
he still ensured that his children were of

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.740
pure Valyrian descent.
He had an older sister, Visenya, and a younger

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:14.630
sister, Rhaenys.
According to Valyrian and Targaryen tradition,

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.530
Aegon married within the family;
however, instead of taking only one sister

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:22.370
to wife, as had been common, he married both
of them.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.659
Aegon was tall, broad-shouldered and powerful
in appearance,

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:32.130
with purple eyes and short-cut silver-gold
hair. He was very charismatic and commanding.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:36.230
During his Conquest he typically wore a shirt
of black scales into battle

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.909
and wielded Valyrian steel sword Blackfyre.
His crown was a simple circlet of Valyrian

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:48.409
steel, set with big square-cut rubies.
Aegon fathered two sons with his sister-wives.

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:51.730
His older son, Aenys, was born to Rhaenys
in 7 AC,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:58.430
and in 12 AC, Visenya bore his younger son
Maegor, later known as "Maegor the Cruel".

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:03.810
But back to Aegon's early days. The first
major event in his life was helping end the

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.400
attempt by Volantis to conquer the other Free
Cities,

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.269
using his dragon to support the forces of
Braavos, Tyrosh and the Westerosi Storm King

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:17.790
in driving the Volantenes from Lys and Myr.
In doing so, he confirmed that he had no interest

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:22.909
in reforging a Valyrian empire in Essos.
Aegon then began planning the invasion of

00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:28.040
Westeros long before launching the attack,
spending time incognito visiting Westerosi

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.040
cities and castles
and gaining intelligence on different houses,

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.380
their lords and their vassals.
He was helped in the planning by his half-brother

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:42.100
born out of wedlock, Orys Baratheon,
his most loyal ally and vassal, his best friend

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.350
and the first Hand of the King.
When he King of the Stormlands, Argilac the

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:50.750
Arrogant offered Aegon an alliance against
Harren the Black, offering his daughter's

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.319
hand in marriage to cement the deal, Aegon
declined

00:03:54.319 --> 00:04:00.220
and instead offered Orys's hand in marriage.
Argilac took that as an insult and cut off

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:04.629
the hands of Aegon's envoy.
Aegon used this as a justification for his

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:08.610
invasion of Westeros.
Aegon, his two sister-wives and their three

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:14.579
dragons led a scant few thousand troops in
invading the entire continent of Westeros.

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:18.180
Aegon fortified his initial landing point
at the northern shore of the mouth of the

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.970
Blackwater River, strategically very defensible
position protected to the east and south by

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.110
water,
and surrounded by open plains which would

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:33.240
expose any attacking army long before it arrived.
Shortly after landing, his sister-wife Visenya

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.940
crowned him King of All Westeros and Shield
of His People, titles he later discarded after

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.960
his second coronation in Oldtown.
Despite being vastly outnumbered, Aegon was

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.530
able to secure victory after victory using
his dragons.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:52.639
The Targaryen siblings departed the Aegonfort,
with Aegon marching northwest into the riverlands

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:57.800
to confront Harren Hoare. Edmyn Tully, Lord
of Riverrun, declared for Aegon

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.250
and led the Riverlords in revolt against the
ruling ironborn.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:08.190
When Harren refused to yield Harrenhal, Aegon
attacked a gigantic new castle with Balerion,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.789
and House Hoare was extinguished with the
burning of Harrenhal.

00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:14.881
The next day Aegon named Edmyn as Lord Paramount
of the Trident.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:19.350
Meanwhile, Rhaenys and Orys defeated the Durrandons
in the Last Storm,

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:23.389
while Visenya fought the Arryns and secured
the Crackclaw Point.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:28.530
After regathering at Stoney Sept, the Targaryen
siblings advanced against the larger host

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:34.539
of the Two Kings, King Mern Gardener of the
Reach and King Loren Lannister of the Rock.

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:38.930
The Targaryen dragons (Balerion, Meraxes,
and Vhagar) allowed Aegon to achieve a great

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:44.310
victory at the Field of Fire, which resulted
in the death of Mern IX Gardener, and the

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:50.010
surrender of Loren I Lannister. Aegon then
marched for Highgarden, where he named Harlan

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:55.949
Tyrell as Lord Paramount after the castle's
surrender. The Targaryens again reunited to

00:05:55.949 --> 00:05:59.620
face the host of Torrhen Stark, the King in
the North,

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:04.250
but Torrhen chose to kneel to Aegon along
the Trident instead of fighting a battle

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.360
and sacrificing dozens of thousands of Northmen
for the lost cause.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.370
Visenya returned to the Vale, where she achieved
the surrender of the Arryns,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:17.389
while Rhaenys flew to Dorne in an unsuccessful
mission to make the Martells bow.

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:23.259
Aegon, meanwhile, marched to Oldtown, which
was surrendered to him by Lord Manfred Hightower

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:27.900
upon the advice of the High Septon. Within
the Starry Sept, the High Septon declared

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:32.080
Aegon to be the King of the Andals, the Rhoynar,
and the First Men,

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:35.090
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms, and Protector
of the Realm.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:40.500
Aegon chose to make his seat King's Landing,
a new settlement growing around the Aegonfort.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.259
He took the swords of his defeated enemies,
forging them into the Iron Throne.

00:06:45.259 --> 00:06:48.080
Aegon also began what would become known as
the small council,

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:53.570
as well as that of the Hand of the King, with
Lord Orys Baratheon becoming his first Hand.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.080
Aegon's first established law was the King's
Peace,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.100
which forbids conflict in the realm without
the leave of the Iron Throne.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.830
Aegon treated the defeated lords with respect
and allowed each region to retain its own

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.110
laws and customs. Aegon often traveled the
realm with six maesters

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:13.820
who educated him on each region's local customs
and history.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.530
In 2 AC, Aegon turned his attention to the
Iron Islands,

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:21.889
where the ironborn had been fighting for two
years over the kingship.

00:07:21.889 --> 00:07:27.570
Aegon landed on Great Wyk with Balerion and
a war fleet to deal with the contenders.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.340
Aegon personally cut down Qhorin Volmark with
Blackfyre,

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.629
while the priest-king Lodos walked into the
sea, drowning himself.

00:07:34.629 --> 00:07:39.430
The other contenders quickly bent the knee.
Aegon allowed the ironborn to name their own

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.539
lord paramount,
for which the ironborn chose Vickon Greyjoy

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:47.090
as Lord of the Iron Islands.
Despite a highly successful reign, Aegon did

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:51.560
face considerable problems
and none were as difficult to deal with as

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:56.110
the First Dornish War.
In 3 AC Aegon turned his attention back on

00:07:56.110 --> 00:08:01.120
Dorne, the only kingdom remaining unconquered.
He first decided to try and bring Dorne under

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.280
the rule of the Iron Throne through diplomacy,
after a year of negotiations and no progress

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:12.440
to show for it although, Aegon decided to
take Dorne by force of arms. In 4 AC Aegon

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.720
launched a new invasion, continuing the Wars
of Conquest.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.979
Although initially the conquest of Dorne seemed
to succeed, it unraveled quickly

00:08:20.979 --> 00:08:27.070
and the First Dornish War prolonged and lasted
for nine years, and knew many deaths and tragedies.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:31.620
One of these tragedies was the capture and
mutilation of Aegon's friend and Hand of the

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.450
King,
Lord Orys Baratheon, by the Wyl of Wyl.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:41.040
Following his release from two years of captivity,
Orys returned home lacking a swordhand.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:46.880
Aegon, intent on revenge, released his dragons
and burned the castles of defiant Dornish

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.410
lords.
In 7 AC, Aegon became a father for the first

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:55.380
time, when his younger sister-wife Rhaenys
gave birth to a son: Aenys.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:09:00.310
The greatest loss Aegon faced was the death
of Queen Rhaenys Targaryen at Hellholt in

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.590
10 AC,
when Meraxes fell from the sky (with Rhaenys

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.030
upon her back)
after a shot from a scorpion took the dragon

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:11.080
in the eye.
The war took a different turn after this.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:16.270
Aegon's fury and grief at the loss of his
wife was such that he headed for Dorne himself.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:21.180
Accompanied by Visenya, the last two Targaryens
rained fire upon the desert strongholds

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:25.740
to break the Dornish. The next two years were
known as the Dragon's Wroth,

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.040
a period when every Dornish castle felt the
fury of the dragonriders.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:34.050
The only castle spared was Sunspear, the seat
of House Martell,

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.530
in hopes that the Dornish would turn against
their liege lords.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:44.410
The strategy failed and Dorne remained unconquered.
In 11 AC, Queen Visenya announced her pregnancy,

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.770
and the next year she gave birth to Aegon's
second son, Maegor.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:53.730
When Princess Meria Martell died in 13 AC,
her son, Prince Nymor, sued for peace, having

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.700
grown weary of war.
He sent his daughter, Deria with the skull

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.450
of Meraxes and a letter with her, to King's
Landing to treat with the Conqueror.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:07.390
The peace demanded by Dorne was peace between
two sovereign kingdoms, not between a liege

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:12.360
and his vassal. Although Aegon heard her out
(against the advice of his advisors, such

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:17.470
as Orys and Visenya), he apparently decided
to refuse the request for peace.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:22.100
Before he could speak, Deria mounted the Iron
Throne and placed the letter from her father

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:27.990
in his hand. What was in the letter is unknown,
but Aegon's hand was so clenched around it

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:33.190
that it started to bleed. He burned the letter
and left on Balerion for Dragonstone.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:38.020
The next morning, he returned and signed the
peace treaty proposed by the Prince of Dorne,

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:43.110
recognizing it as a sovereign kingdom.
Historians suspect that Nymor had revealed

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.640
to Aegon that Rhaenys was still alive and
badly injured from falling off Meraxes and

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.220
that he would end her suffering if the Conqueror
agreed to peace.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:57.160
However I do not believe this to be true
because Aegon kept good relations with Princess

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:01.420
Deria afterward.
Perhaps his sister survived the fall and she

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:06.340
delivered her to Aegon on Dragonstone.
He even visited Sunspear with his eldest son,

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:10.630
Prince Aenys, in 23 AC
to celebrate the tenth anniversary of the

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:14.800
peace between the Iron Throne and Dorne.
Anyways, the Conqueror was almost killed by

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:19.960
assassins in the streets of King's Landing
and was only saved by Visenya. This led to

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:23.800
creation of the Kingsguard,
with its first members chosen by Visenya to

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.830
protect her brother-husband with their lives.
The remaining twenty-four years of Aegon's

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.670
reign were peaceful,
so much that the last two decades of his reign

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:37.670
were later called the Dragon's Peace,
by the maesters of the Citadel. He spent much

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:42.150
of his time consolidating his power by traveling
throughout the Seven Kingdoms and building

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:47.280
his capital at King's Landing.
In 37 AC on Dragonstone, while telling his

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:52.750
two eldest grandsons Aegon and Viserys the
tales of his conquest at the Painted Table,

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:58.640
Aegon died from a stroke at the age of sixty-four.
Aegon was cremated on Dragonstone, and his

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:04.440
funeral pyre was set aflame by Vhagar.
Blackfyre was burned along with him, but later

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:09.740
retrieved from the pyre by Maegor.
That is the story of a legendary, ear-mythical

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:13.110
figure, Aegon the Conqueror.
Let me know your thoughts about all of this

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:17.130
in the comment section down below.
Once again, House of the Dragon, a Game of

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:22.350
Thrones prequel about House Targaryen is coming
in 2022 on HBO.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:25.910
Thank you so much for watching, if you enjoyed
this video please give it a big thumbs up

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:37.700
and I hope to see you in the next one.
Peace!

